    {
      "instance_id": "scout_journal",
      "type": "readable",
      "model": "assets/models/props/lectern_ledger.glb",
      "pos": [
        -19.2,
        0.0,
        -2.4
      ],
      "rot_y": 120.0,
      "prompt": "Read Kaelen's Field Journal",
      "title": "Field Journal of Kaelen, Ashbound",
      "text": "Day 41. The boundary stone of Oakhallow again. Four hundred and twelve souls, it says. I count the foundations in the bracken: none. I count the wells: one, dry, with a bucket still on the rope.\n\nDay 43. The Annex has sunk. Its upper offices fell into something older underneath, and the stairs now go down further than the building ever went up. The skeletons inside still keep office hours.\n\nDay 44. A traveller from Bellwether asked what we Ashbound are for. I told her: somebody has to remember things on purpose."
    },
    {
      "instance_id": "baggy_case_board",
      "type": "readable",
      "model": "assets/models/props/lectern_ledger.glb",
      "pos": [
        10.2,
        0.0,
        -6.4
      ],
      "rot_y": -60.0,
      "prompt": "Read Baggy's Case Notes",
      "title": "CASE FILE #1: THE MISSING TOWN",
      "text": "Property of BAGGY, Private Eye (Licence pending. Licence fee also pending.)\n\nSUSPECTS:\n1. The hedge. Too neat. Hiding something.\n2. The Bureau. Too many forms. Hiding EVERYTHING.\n3. A goat. (Probably not involved. Looked at me funny.)\n4. Myself? (Ruled out. I have an alibi: I was here. Wait.)\n\nCLUES:\n- Boundary stone says 412 people. I count 0 people. Discrepancy of 412. Very large discrepancy.\n- One dry well. One bucket. Somebody was thirsty, once.\n- I remember a girl with flour on her nose who gave me a sweet roll. I was seven. Nobody else remembers her. CENTRAL MYSTERY.\n\nTHEORY: A whole town was erased by someone with very good handwriting.\n\nNEXT STEPS: Find the town. Find the girl. Find my other glove."
    },
    {
      "instance_id": "sabrino_stash",
      "type": "chest",
      "model": "assets/models/props/treasure_chest.glb",
      "pos": [
        -12.0,
