        "core:item.mana_potion",
        "core:item.mana_potion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "instance_id": "sabrino_note",
      "type": "readable",
      "model": "",
      "pos": [
        -10.4,
        0.95,
        12.4
      ],
      "prompt": "Read the Garlic-Scented Note",
      "title": "A Note, Weighed Down with a Clove of Garlic",
      "text": "To Whoever Finds My Hat,\n\nThe Bureau is onto me again. They have charged me with 1,412 counts of Unlicensed Fireballing, which is a lie. It was 1,413. They always forget the one at the wedding.\n\nI am leaving the hat and my good grimoire here under the pine, because a witch on the run cannot also carry a hat that tall. It keeps catching on tavern doors. Very bad for a dramatic exit.\n\nTake them. Wear the hat crooked, it works better. Cast the fireball from FAR away. Further than that. No, further.\n\nAnd if a nice man in a long coat asks where I went, tell him dinner is at eight, as always, and he is still invited.\n\nCiao,\nSabrino\n\nP.S. Do not let anyone tell you that pineapple goes on anything. That is the real war crime.",
      "quest_id": "core:quest.dinner_at_eight",
      "set_stage": 0,
      "set_flag": "sabrino_in_town"
    },
    {
